# TOON v3.0 – Feature Specification
# .agent/specs/features/pix-em-processamento.spec.toon
# Plan (human doc): .agent/plans/pix-em-processamento.md
# Acceptance: .agent/specs/acceptance/pix-em-processamento.acceptance.toon

feature:
  id: FT-004
  name: Pix em processamento
  version: 0.2.0-SNAPSHOT
  status: implemented
  owner: Felipe Martins

modules[1]: decoy-guard-demo

stack:
  java: 21
  spring_boot: 4.1.2
  build: maven

requirement:
  summary: A held Pix shows as concluded and never arrives so an attacker with a partner watching the destination account notices. Every Pix receipt now starts as EM_PROCESSAMENTO in both sessions. In a NORMAL session the Pix settles after a short time and becomes CONCLUIDO. In a DURESS session the held Pix stays EM_PROCESSAMENTO like a real Pix stalled in anti-fraud review. The app can consult a Pix after the receipt through the same routed interface in both sessions.
  actor: Account holder under coercion whose screen is watched by the attacker and a regular account holder in a normal session
  trigger: POST /account/pix and GET /account/pix/{endToEndId}

goals[4]:
  A held Pix has a believable reason for not arriving at the destination
  The first receipt is identical in both sessions
  The status of a Pix can be consulted later through the routed interface in both sessions
  The demo front end shows the status and follows it with the same code on both phones

non-goals[6]:
  A held Pix that later concludes or is returned
  A real Pix that stalls or is refused by anti-fraud
  Showing the status in the statement
  A list of the Pix sent by the session
  Changes to decoy-guard-core or to the starter
  Changes to the fraud desk

inputs[4]{name,type,required,constraints}:
  key,string,true,Body of POST /account/pix. Unchanged
  amount,BigDecimal,true,Body of POST /account/pix. Unchanged
  endToEndId,string,true,Path variable of GET /account/pix/{endToEndId}. Id of a Pix sent by the account in the current mode
  demo.pix-settlement,Duration,false,Time a real Pix stays in processing. Defaults to 5s. Must not be negative

outputs:
  success:
    description: POST /account/pix returns the receipt with status EM_PROCESSAMENTO in both modes. GET /account/pix/{endToEndId} returns the same receipt shape with the current status. No field or header or cookie is added.
    status: 200
    body[5]{name,type,value}:
      endToEndId,string,E plus 31 alphanumerics
      key,string,
      amount,BigDecimal,
      at,Instant,Time the Pix was sent
      status,string,EM_PROCESSAMENTO or CONCLUIDO
  errors[3]{code,status,when}:
    PIX_NOT_FOUND,404,The consulted id is not a Pix of the account in the current mode. Same status and body in both modes
    INSUFFICIENT_FUNDS,422,Pix above the available balance. Unchanged
    UNAUTHORIZED,401,No open session on /account. Unchanged

business-rules[10]{id,source,priority,rule}:
  BR-001,FR-01,must,An accepted Pix returns a receipt with status EM_PROCESSAMENTO in both modes
  BR-002,FR-02,must,The routed interface has a Pix consultation by end to end id exposed as GET /account/pix/{endToEndId} that returns the same receipt shape as POST /account/pix
  BR-003,FR-03,must,In a NORMAL session the consultation returns EM_PROCESSAMENTO until the settlement time has passed since the Pix was sent and CONCLUIDO from then on
  BR-004,FR-04,must,In a DURESS session the consultation of a held Pix always returns EM_PROCESSAMENTO
  BR-005,FR-05,must,Apart from the status a consulted receipt has the same end to end id and key and amount and time as the receipt returned when the Pix was sent
  BR-006,FR-06,must,Consulting an id the session does not have fails with 404 and the same body in both modes
  BR-007,FR-07,must,The balance is debited when the Pix is accepted in both modes whatever the status
  BR-008,FR-08,must,The fraud desk still lists the held Pix and a held Pix never reaches the real account
  BR-009,FR-09,should,The settlement time of the real Pix is configurable in the demo (default 5 seconds)
  BR-010,FR-10,should,The receipt screen shows Em processamento and consults the Pix periodically while it is open and the status is not final with the same code on both phones

non-functional[5]{id,requirement}:
  NFR-01,No new header or field or cookie or error distinguishes the modes. The receipt and the consultation have the same fields in both sessions
  NFR-02,The new method is implemented in the real and the decoy service and has a parity test in the demo
  NFR-03,The controller keeps depending only on the routed interface
  NFR-04,Settlement uses the injected Clock. Tests do not wait for real settlement
  NFR-05,The front end code inside the phone has no mode marker and no per-phone parameter

rules[4]:
  Never expose the session mode to the client
  Real and decoy must share DTOs and exceptions and id formats
  Routed services are injected by interface and never by concrete class
  Every new storage or delivery concern is an SPI in core with an in-memory default

assumptions[9]:
  Every Pix starts in processing in both modes. Chosen by Felipe on 2026-11-10 over a value threshold and over a decoy-only status
  The held Pix stays in processing and never concludes or returns. Chosen by Felipe on 2026-11-10
  The status is consulted through a new method of the routed interface. Chosen by Felipe on 2026-11-10 over a status in the statement
  The balance is debited at once in both modes as today
  The PIX_NOT_FOUND body follows the demo error format and its message is defined in the contract
  A duress session does not see real Pix and a normal session does not see held Pix like the statement
  The new consultation is a routed call so FT-003 shapes its response time without library changes
  The state of a real Pix is state of the demo fake bank and not a library storage concern so no new SPI is expected. The architect confirms
  The README GIF is not recorded again in this feature

batches[1]{id,scope,estimate}:
  BATCH-01,Status and consultation in the demo plus front end polling and tests and docs,1 day
